Keep the trailing newline when a stat format ends in a lone '%'.
stat prints a newline after each -c format, but when the format ended
in a '%' with no directive letter after it, print_it() printed the '%'
and stopped, so "stat -c 'abc%' FILE" printed "abc%" with no newline
and ran the output for the next file onto the same line. Print the '%'
and then go on to the end of the format as usual, which prints the
newline, as coreutils stat does.

---
 coreutils/stat.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/stat.c
+++ b/coreutils/stat.c
@@ -476,7 +476,8 @@
 		b = p + 1;
 		switch (*p) {
 		case '\0':
-			b = NULL;
+			/* format ends in '%': print it, then the newline */
+			b = p;
 			/* fall through */
 		case '%':
 			bb_putchar('%');
